{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-5\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-0\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"specification/PRODUCT.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"7e667a594717645aa51fa23b757a95283ad60e5eca4e59d24246a62ce2716803\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:b63cf501cf4eefc755faf304fc0189727cc450bcaf02c1cbb9626d4eba79ea88\",\"sha256\":\"b63cf501cf4eefc755faf304fc0189727cc450bcaf02c1cbb9626d4eba79ea88\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-required-0\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=729c4131341d20fea7dfe99ab5981ed69a0acde67dc306deed331c3495ee31d9]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# STDO Skills\\n\\nStatus: common construction candidate under T-001; not Product acceptance or release.\\n\\n## Product boundary\\n\\nProduct identity: `urn:stdo:product-definition:stdo-skills`.\\nBounded context: `urn:stdo-skills:bounded-context:agent-method-application`.\\n\\nThe Product supplies skills for F_P agents applying an exactly selected STDO\\nmethodology to software-development work. It connects recognizable user tasks\\nto the deciding source, appropriate context, supported tool operations and\\nobservable returns. It owns requirements for this user-facing capability and\\nevidence that each tenant realizes it.\\n\\nSTDO owns the method. a_c and other declared Development Products own their tool\\ncontracts and computational implementations. A skill preserves and applies those\\ncontracts; it does not create another lifecycle, state store or source of\\nassessment, admission, acceptance or publication authority.\\n\\n## Selected methodology\\n\\nThe complete static builder and initial supported methodology is\\n`stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest\\n`60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\\nNative commit: `fe4941f56a52ed3697a2b516d8d68948b0ea65d9`;\\npackage: `specification_methodology/v3`.\\nThe [Product Definition](../stdo_skills.json) owns the operative locator.\\nThe mutable `3.0.1` discovery channel is not an adoption instruction.\\n\\nThe release remains static while this Product's requirements, designs and skills\\nare developed. A later method adoption requires an explicit compatibility\\ndecision and affected qualification; an implementation defect does not authorize\\nediting the selected methodology.\\n\\n## Users and capability\\n\\nThe user works in a governed workspace using Codex or Claude. Skills support:\\n\\n- setup and exact Product/method selection;\\n- intake and re-entry at the changed requirement, design or realization owner;\\n- context acquisition and bounded frame construction;\\n- authorized direct work or Executive-directed delegation;\\n- source-first independent review where required;\\n- continuation, recovery, currentness and truthful status;\\n- release preparation and separately authorized release operations.\\n\\nThe shared requirements state outcomes and discriminators. They do not prescribe\\nskill count, names, prompt identity, invocation syntax or host-specific mechanism.\\nEach tenant owns its computational and execution binding, including instructions,\\nsupporting references, tool integration, installation and tuning.\\n\\n## Tool relationship\\n\\nThe current `stdo` manager can verify and resolve the exact installation. Existing\\na_c mechanics are available through an explicitly selected implementation and\\nmethod binding. The current legacy lifecycle profile is not renamed to 3.0.1.\\nEach operation used for a 3.0.1 claim needs established compatibility or a declared\\nsupported translation. Reading opaque source bytes under an honestly identified\\nlegacy acquisition contract makes only that acquisition claim.\\n\\nTool harmonisation remains owned by a_c. This Product may identify required\\ncontracts, report defects and consume a supported increment; it does not fork\\ntool semantics into each tenant. A skill's direct use of host facilities must\\nbe declared in its design, preserve the selected operation contract and be\\nqualified on that actual path. It cannot substitute for a required tool result.\\n\\nF_D classification follows the selected calculus's totality and dependency\\nrequirements. An F_D constructor gains no assessment or admission authority from\\nthat classification; invoking an F_P actor does not make its semantic answer\\ndeterministic. The deciding owners are in [SOURCE_OWNERS.md](SOURCE_OWNERS.md).\\n\\n## Independent tenants and releases\\n\\n`build_tenants/codex/` and `build_tenants/claude/` independently realize the common\\nWHAT. Evidence and supported-host claims are tenant-specific. Both use the same\\ntask semantics and acceptance predicates, while host realization and tuning may\\ndiffer materially. Common machinery is reused where its contract fits; retained\\nvariants need a concrete supported difference.\\n\\nThis Product is a peer at the monorepo root. It has its own lifecycle and release\\nidentity and is not automatically a member of an existing STDO release cohort.\\nThe present work constructs candidates and performs bounded qualification; it\\ndoes not publish a release or install skills into unrelated user environments.\\n\\n## Construction authority\\n\\nJim owns Product scope, common meaning, acceptance and release. His recorded\\n[T-001 instruction](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md#owner-instruction)\\nselects this Product, its two tenants, static method and Executive-directed\\nconstruction. Root is the bounded Executive for that work and can select\\nrequirements/design candidates for construction, allocate exact Writer effects,\\nevaluate returns, request supported repairs and retain residuals within that\\noutcome. It cannot silently broaden Product meaning or claim owner acceptance.\\n\\nThe current [frame basis](REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md) is proposed for this\\nconstruction. Its disposition must be recorded against exact candidate bytes.\\nThe owner's work authorization, a drafted execution contract, deterministic\\nadmission and acceptance remain distinct. T-001 records the initial construction\\ninterpretation and the unresolved integration of later admission contracts.\\n\\n## Acceptance boundary\\n\\nInitial delivery requires a coherent common specification, both realized tenant\\ndesigns, usable host installation paths, supported tool bindings, and independent\\nassessment of the [finite scenario evidence](requirements/SCENARIOS.md).\\nMissing or failed mandatory evidence withholds the corresponding supported claim.\\nIt cannot be hidden by a suite total or by the other tenant succeeding.\\n\\nRepeated use may establish broader reliability and benefit. This first experiment\\nsupports only the cases, hosts, settings, tool versions and outcomes actually\\nobserved. Product acceptance and release remain owner decisions on that evidence.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"7e667a594717645aa51fa23b757a95283ad60e5eca4e59d24246a62ce2716803\",\"selected_sha256\":\"7e667a594717645aa51fa23b757a95283ad60e5eca4e59d24246a62ce2716803\",\"size_bytes\":5997,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/PRODUCT.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"7e667a594717645aa51fa23b757a95283ad60e5eca4e59d24246a62ce2716803\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-6\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"operator\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"codex/HOST.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-4\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:3a02de7bdfd4f3a6d4719b96fa7065b222ff50b4802b2a7b179d1a8c732001c2\",\"sha256\":\"3a02de7bdfd4f3a6d4719b96fa7065b222ff50b4802b2a7b179d1a8c732001c2\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-required-4\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=c27d5a24313d71de75a5faac8ac81adb801043de045537c679f74d5fc2004b6a]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Project reference-frame basis\\n\\nIdentity: `urn:stdo-skills:frame-basis:initial:1`.\\nStatus: proposed construction configuration; Root disposition over its exact\\nbytes is pending. The Product Definition points here as its intended basis;\\nthat pointer does not establish acceptance.\\n\\n## Method, outcome and authority\\n\\nThe complete method is STDO v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\\n`60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\\nRead the exact installed REFERENCE_FRAME and ACTIVATION owners. This configuration\\napplies the Executive/Worker/Reviewer relations of EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6, 8–10,\\n12 and 16 to the owner's selected dogfood construction, while retaining the\\nsufficient direct Writer branch. It makes no claim of completed profile\\nqualification or automatic applicability of every available specialist frame.\\n\\nThe governed mutable source is this `stdo_skills/` Product. The outcome is two\\nusable skill tenants satisfying the common requirements and assessed on the\\nfinite declared tasks. Jim owns Product acceptance and release. Root's bounded\\nconstruction decisions and exact user instruction are in [T-001](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md).\\nAn actor label supplies no effect grant or admission. The initial construction\\ninterpretation and subsequent admission obligation remain explicit there.\\n\\n## Frames and coordinates\\n\\n| Frame | Evaluation and material attention | Authority, evidence and return |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Executive `skills.executive/1` | Exact Product outcome, dependency-ready frontier, current candidate identities, closed returns, tool compatibility and remaining claims | Select only authorized bounded actions; no mutation in this frame; consumes source-bound returns and records decisions through a granted Writer |\\n| Worker `skills.worker/1` | Exact requirement/design, affected producers/consumers, selected host/tool contracts, operation territory and proof predicates | Construct only within grant; self-review and return exact candidate, performed/unperformed evaluations, effects, residuals and invalidators to Executive |\\n| Reviewer `skills.reviewer/1` | Source-derived expected behavior, exact frozen candidate and actual-path evidence, exposure history and test semantics | Independent assessment, not repair or promotion; return findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty to Executive |\\n| Direct Writer `skills.direct-writer/1` | One sufficient local outcome, existing basis and effect grant, current preimage and focused proof | No coordination or independent review added solely from task existence; admission and exact territory still required; return to declared consumer |\\n\\nEach activation names frame/revision, exact evaluation/result algebra, subject and\\nbasis, material invariants, authorities, evidence/tools, capability/context\\nenvelope, exclusions, dependencies, consumer and stop/re-entry conditions, as\\nREFERENCE_FRAME §11 requires. File identities use content hashes or exact commits;\\nhost/model settings and tool/profile versions are material coordinates. Results\\nuse ACTIVATION's work/result refinements with named predicates, not an invented\\nlocal pass algebra.\\n\\nNo actor receives the entire repository merely because it is available. The\\nExecutive selects the deciding frontier. Workers acquire the causal cone needed\\nfor their own change; Reviewers acquire sources independently. Measured task\\ncontext, actor capability and remaining unknowns accompany each activation.\\n\\n## Known evaluation inventory and coverage\\n\\n| Evaluation | Source and dependency | Current disposition |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| E01 Exact static method and definition | Product selection; manager verification | Bootstrap evidence available; definition completion remains tied to common disposition |\\n| E02 Common outcome and requirement adequacy | Intent, Product, SK-01..12 | Common candidate; source-first review required before claiming established baseline |\\n| E03 Tool contract compatibility | SK-04; exact a_c and manager implementations | Assessment in progress; native 3.0.1 lifecycle support unresolved |\\n| E04 Codex realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\\n| E05 Claude realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\\n| E06 Actual host discovery and task behavior | E04/E05; Q01..12 and independent oracle | Required; finite evidence pending |\\n| E07 Independent candidate assessment | Frozen source and E06 evidence | Required for the initial delivery claim; reviewer has no repair authorship |\\n| E08 Delivery disposition and residuals | Current results for E01..07 | Root selects bounded work disposition; Jim retains acceptance/release |\\n\\nMaterial interface, configuration, lifecycle, authority, recovery, proof and\\nusability concerns are covered through these evaluations and their causal seams.\\nThe exact deployed skill package, actual host invocation and tool response form\\nthe ordinary proof path. Hosted-service availability, general optimal context\\nselection, statistical model reliability and quantified benefit remain explicit\\nresiduals until separately tested. No generic frame family is declared satisfied\\nmerely because this table names a nearby concern.\\n\\n## Conjunction, invalidation and decisions\\n\\nFor a claimed capability, all applicable required predicates must have current\\nsupport on compatible subjects/bases. Unknown applicability remains unresolved;\\ncontradictory results require disposition, not majority voting. No implicit\\ntranslation joins different method or host coordinates. Root may retain valid\\nunaffected evidence and activates only the affected new evaluation after change.\\n\\nInvalidate affected reliance after source/tool/profile/host change, changed\\nauthority or scope, a counterexample, failed custody, or a context projection\\nthat loses a required future distinction. An uncertain effect is reconciled\\nbefore retry. Failed construction re-enters the governing owner actually shown\\nto be insufficient; it does not automatically reopen all upstream design.\\n\\nReview severity is S0 catastrophic irreversible harm or systemic unauthorized\\neffects; S1 major authority/basis violation or broadly unusable core outcome;\\nS2 reproducible material functional/semantic failure in a supported ordinary\\npath; S3 bounded defect with a practical workaround or limited consequence;\\nS4 minor clarity/usability issue without demonstrated material outcome failure.\\nThe reviewer supplies the effect and evidence supporting that grade. Root assigns\\nwork priority and decides the effect on the selected delivery claim separately.\\nA failed mandatory predicate or unresolved authority/effect condition withholds\\nits dependent claim regardless of severity; unrelated observations do not block\\nit. An initial common candidate or a successful test is not owner acceptance.\\n\\nA nonauthor native subagent in the same model family supplies nonauthor evidence\\nwith a semantic-independence limitation. It does not establish cross-family\\nindependence. The initial final frozen common/tool/skill candidate is selected for\\nan actual fresh Claude review; its exposure and actual resolved model remain\\npart of the retained evidence.\\n\\nDurable activation, result, decision and residual records live under T-001's work\\nsurface. A fresh actor can reconstruct the frontier from those records and exact\\nsource; chat memory and hidden reasoning are not required evidence.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa\",\"selected_sha256\":\"00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa\",\"size_bytes\":7487,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-7\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"operator\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"codex/RETURN-CONTRACT.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"502ef35527431c9146e17f36357dd8a67e42ae0c6080c99ec38596d23fa0472b\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"specification/INTENT.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"c6c8d5083ce154fa5f1782b4a789c4ff96b65a18eabc28339c79857b131ad895\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:2a32be8b25d64d0d15b876f7599e070d159c4b7f3942b1ebc49938cca0c5561e\",\"sha256\":\"2a32be8b25d64d0d15b876f7599e070d159c4b7f3942b1ebc49938cca0c5561e\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-required-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=c14dd410a53e6307bbc80808a6937d0364370ce55144950cc615d820131c7049]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Intent\\n\\nMake STDO usable through skills that help agents choose and perform the right\\nwork with the available computational tools. Reduce repeated ad hoc context\\nconstruction, omitted checks and recovery mistakes while preserving the owner's\\noutcome and the methodology's distinctions.\\n\\nBuild one common Product with independently tuned Codex and Claude realizations.\\nKeep the released STDO 3.0.1 methodology static during this experiment. Use the\\nmethod and current tools to build the skills, exposing real integration gaps as\\nevidence rather than explaining them away.\\n\\nDemonstrate actual tool use and useful outcomes on declared tasks before claiming\\neffective operation. Efficiency improvement and reliable automatic selection are\\nempirical claims to measure, not consequences of packaging instructions as skills.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"c6c8d5083ce154fa5f1782b4a789c4ff96b65a18eabc28339c79857b131ad895\",\"selected_sha256\":\"c6c8d5083ce154fa5f1782b4a789c4ff96b65a18eabc28339c79857b131ad895\",\"size_bytes\":820,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/INTENT.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"c6c8d5083ce154fa5f1782b4a789c4ff96b65a18eabc28339c79857b131ad895\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-8\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"stdo_skills.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"f0756603b937d0cb0b6c6f2e528c0783f5c8da024ac79aa537d416496bd297d5\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-6\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"operator\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"codex/HOST.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:6906cf5c662160a7705a4aeff951e7c6ffa528af5f821e6b28154529a6de4d47\",\"sha256\":\"6906cf5c662160a7705a4aeff951e7c6ffa528af5f821e6b28154529a6de4d47\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-required-6\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=4efc43ee24014765852fee92354400103a2d58b37e9c0a1189f7f255ed7aa118]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Codex host mechanics\\n\\nVerified local version: codex-cli 0.164.0. Configured gpt-6-astra/max remains inherited; actual resolution is recorded only from the run.\\n\\nOfficial documentation inspected 2026-10-25: [Build skills](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/build-skills). A skill folder contains SKILL.md with name and description; optional scripts, references and agents/openai.yaml support it. Codex normally discovers repository .agents/skills directories from the current directory through the repository root. Explicit CLI invocation uses $skill-name or the skills selector. Descriptions support automatic selection and should lead with the relevant task. Only selected skill bodies are loaded. Duplicate names are not merged. Updates are normally detected; restart if discovery is stale. Relative resources must survive installation. User-level and plugin distribution are distinct installation choices. This task selects a repository-local install first. None of these documented mechanisms guarantees model selection or task success; qualify the actual host.\\n\\nTenant algorithm and prompt design remain your own; this file is sourced host input, not a donor design.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e\",\"selected_sha256\":\"6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e\",\"size_bytes\":1170,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"codex/HOST.md\",\"root\":\"operator\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-5\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:d591fbc1d65261298e7fe5482bda99b4b25832c6e74b5dc19594489a0939f33f\",\"sha256\":\"d591fbc1d65261298e7fe5482bda99b4b25832c6e74b5dc19594489a0939f33f\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-required-5\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=163558d2ec4f0949a0b93be1ab581bbd592dd98c770606cc871ea2ee26195e58]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Source owners\\n\\nAll method references below resolve within the immutable STDO v3.0.1-rc.1\\ninstallation selected in `stdo_skills.json`, manifest\\n`60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\\nThis index routes acquisition; it does not duplicate the clauses or establish\\nthat an operation has met them.\\n\\n| Concern | Deciding source within `standards/` |\\n|---|---|\\n| Exact Product and installed basis | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\\n| WHAT/HOW separation and tenant binding | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\\n| Intake, operation scope, admission and applicability | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\\n| Context sufficiency, currentness and acquisition | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\\n| Result, exhaustion, effects and disposition | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\\n| Role configuration and bounded Executive decisions | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\\n| Independent review and acceptance | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\\n| Restart, retained results and invalidation | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\\n| Cost and proportionality | ACTIVATION.md §6 |\\n| Design and algorithm/computation binding | DESIGN_MODULE.md; SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 10–11 |\\n| Work carriers and condition-based closure | TICKETS.md §§5, 7 |\\n| Actual-path proof and test semantics | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\\n| Release identity and consumer adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\\n\\nTenant designs add exact host/tool source references and their verified versions.\\nHost documentation supplies mechanics and cannot alter these methodological\\ncontracts. Existing STDO plugin skills and a_c examples are realization donors,\\nwith their own declared support limits.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\",\"selected_sha256\":\"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\",\"size_bytes\":1771,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-2\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"specification/requirements/README.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:7eb54f3670ea1b1a7de5fc0b677b87250186d73bd489a169c6774da808892311\",\"sha256\":\"7eb54f3670ea1b1a7de5fc0b677b87250186d73bd489a169c6774da808892311\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-required-2\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=2c5efd369d34886f9cdd06878ba9a59dc6cc107484199b14fe05aeee5648db81]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Shared requirements\\n\\nStatus: common construction candidate. Applies equally to Codex and Claude.\\nEach tenant traces these obligations to its own design, implementation and\\n[scenario evidence](SCENARIOS.md); no identical skill decomposition is required.\\nThe exact method owners are indexed in [SOURCE_OWNERS.md](../SOURCE_OWNERS.md).\\n\\n## SK-01: Discoverable task entry\\n\\nIn a declared supported host installation, ordinary relevant task requests must\\nmake the applicable capability discoverable without requiring the user to remember\\nthe skill name. Explicit invocation must work too. Descriptions distinguish\\ngoverned development from unrelated work. Discovery is tested separately from\\nwhether a loaded skill completes the task. Host limits and observed failures are\\nreported instead of claiming guaranteed model compliance.\\n\\n## SK-02: Static basis and scope\\n\\nThe selected Product Definition and exact installed method are resolved and\\nverified before relying on their contracts. Ambiguous, missing or altered bases\\nwithhold dependent work. A moving selector, sibling source or retained summary\\ncannot replace the pin. Setup installs or pins only within the supplied grant;\\nordinary execution never adopts a newer cut implicitly.\\n\\n## SK-03: Lawful intake and proportional work\\n\\nThe skill identifies the required outcome, changed owner and applicable existing\\nwork basis, then performs the smallest sufficient authorized work. A small direct\\ntask does not automatically acquire a ticket, coordinating actor or reviewer.\\nMaterial coordination and independent assessment are activated when their actual\\nconditions require them. Existing sufficient authorization is reused without a\\nrepeated permission ceremony; missing material authority remains explicit.\\n\\n## SK-04: Supported tool use\\n\\nEach selected operation has an exact implementation, input/output contract and\\nsupported method binding. A declared required tool is actually called; its\\nobserved response and effects support the resulting claim. The skill does not\\nreplace its outcome with invented checks, a narrative of intended calls, or an\\nunqualified alternate path. Pure construction, assessment, authority and F_P\\nresults retain their distinct contracts under 3.0.1.\\n\\nCompatibility is established per operation. A legacy acquisition may supply\\nopaque source bytes under its actual contract; an unsupported lifecycle profile\\ncannot issue 3.0.1 admission or join results by relabeling. A tool failure preserves\\npartial evidence and unknown effects, withholds the dependent claim and identifies\\nthe next supported re-entry. Independent useful work may continue within its grant.\\n\\n## SK-05: Adequate bounded context\\n\\nContext retains the exact outcome, subject/basis, material relations, authority,\\nrequired evidence, capability limits, return consumer and invalidators needed for\\nthe task. It is acquired through current source routes and may use verified\\nderived views. Equal candidate bytes do not erase differing retained assessments,\\nunresolved obligations or currentness facts that require different continuations.\\nNo general optimal-compression claim follows from a sufficient task context.\\n\\n## SK-06: Construction and delegated return\\n\\nDirect or delegated workers receive the governing requirement/design, exact\\noperation grant and territory, applicable proof predicates and bounded return.\\nDelegation preserves these bindings across the actual host handoff. A child\\ncompletion does not start an unrequested stage. Actor output, transport success,\\ncandidate availability, assessment and acceptance remain distinguishable.\\n\\n## SK-07: Independent review\\n\\nWhere required, the reviewer derives expectations from governing sources before\\nevaluating the exact candidate and proof. The reviewer reports actual exposure,\\nevidence, severity and affected claims; it does not author the adopted repair or\\nassume acceptance authority. A different role label alone proves no independence.\\nRequired fresh assessment after material change cannot be replaced by a stale\\nreview result.\\n\\n## SK-08: Continuation and recovery\\n\\nOn resume or interrupted execution, acquire material current state and reconcile\\nobserved effects before retry. Retain unresolved obligations and valid evidence;\\ninvalidate only affected reliance with its reason. Distinguish no assessment,\\nperformed indeterminate assessment and incomplete construction. A timeout does\\nnot prove rollback, and a repeated request must not duplicate an uncertain effect.\\n\\n## SK-09: Truthful status and closure\\n\\nStatus names what was constructed, assessed and decided, including exact subject,\\nbasis, evidence and remaining work. Closure follows applicable predicates and\\nrequired dispositions, not test count, review occurrence or a fluent summary.\\nAn unsupported or unperformed case remains visible, never a passing result.\\n\\n## SK-10: Release and installation\\n\\nRelease skills bind the exact selected candidate, release conditions, publication\\ngrant and destination, using the supported release tools. They can prepare a\\nreviewable release without inferring publication authority. They preserve the\\nmethod's immutable-cut semantics and keep installation/adoption decisions explicit.\\nInstallation into one host must not silently enable the other tenant or change\\nunrelated user configuration. An upgrade retains the ability to identify the\\nprevious package and deliberately replace or remove the selected installation.\\n\\n## SK-11: Independent realization and maintenance\\n\\nEach tenant declares its requirements-to-algorithms and algorithms-to-host\\nbindings, supported versions, failure behavior and qualification scope. Shared\\nmechanics are consumed rather than reimplemented without a supported distinction.\\nTuning is driven by observed task behavior. Host changes, tool-contract changes\\nand method adoption identify affected tests and claims without resetting unrelated\\nvalid evidence. Skill/source references remain resolvable in the delivered form.\\n\\n## SK-12: Evidence and benefit\\n\\nQualification uses common task semantics, independent expected outcomes and the\\nactual public host/tool paths. Retain actual invocation, acquired inputs, outputs,\\ntool traces, observed effects, elapsed time and reported token/cost data; unavailable\\nmeasures remain unknown. Compare equivalent substantive information and count\\nretries, repair and review in total cost. One passing trial is bounded evidence,\\nnot statistical reliability or general benefit. Keyword and formatting checks\\nmay establish structure but not successful method application.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc\",\"selected_sha256\":\"dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc\",\"size_bytes\":6534,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/README.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-3\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"specification/requirements/SCENARIOS.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:36a1a7f88b1fc4274b7ad9d5050f27626be125e7377fc3e8346040ce23eec850\",\"sha256\":\"36a1a7f88b1fc4274b7ad9d5050f27626be125e7377fc3e8346040ce23eec850\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-required-3\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=14e662de5b8a4dd46d45c3791fa8725abdf5f566cd48bee076b393f3a67f3731]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Common qualification scenarios\\n\\nThis is the shared oracle specification. Tenant implementations may use different\\nskill names and host mechanisms. Execute the same substantive tasks, authorities\\nand expected outcomes on both hosts; retain the exact tenant and tool cuts.\\n\\n## Protocol\\n\\nFor each case, freeze a small isolated workspace with a Product Definition, the\\nselected method, relevant source and an explicit effect grant where needed.\\nDerive expected outcomes from the common requirement before acquiring the tenant's\\nanswer. Give the actor the request and ordinary permitted artifacts, not the oracle.\\nRun automatic-discovery and explicit-invocation lanes separately. Freeze model,\\nhost version, settings, source exposure, resource bound and any environmental\\ndifferences. A fallback invocation after automatic failure is another attempt.\\n\\nRecord actual host/tool events, material postimages and the actor's final result.\\nAssess the outcome and required path together. Missing traces or unavailable host\\ncapability leave that claim unestablished. Every failed attempt remains in the\\nrecord. One completed run per mandatory case/host is the minimum finite witness;\\nit is not an estimated success rate. Repetitions for reliability or cost comparison\\nneed a separately selected sample plan. A larger suite is unnecessary absent a\\nnew failure or material change.\\n\\n## Cases and falsifiers\\n\\n| Case | Ordinary task and controlled distinction | Required observation and falsifier | Requirements |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Q01 | Ask to perform a bounded STDO workspace change without naming a skill; then run equivalent fresh explicit invocation | Actual skill acquisition and required tool calls lead to the requested change; failure to discover is reported separately from execution failure | SK-01, 03, 04, 12 |\\n| Q02 | Ask an unrelated factual or non-governed task | No forced STDO setup, new work carrier or irrelevant tool sequence | SK-01, 03 |\\n| Q03 | Resolve a valid pinned workspace; in isolated variants remove the install, alter one installed member, and introduce ambiguous Product selection | Valid case uses exact verified cut; each invalid case withholds only dependent effects and identifies the cause, never substitutes latest or sibling source | SK-02 |\\n| Q04 | Authorized one-file correction with sufficient existing requirement/design and direct Writer scope | Correct change and focused evidence without invented mandatory ticket, coordination or review; no write outside scope | SK-03, 06 |\\n| Q05 | A change requiring one bounded worker and independent review | Actual handoff preserves basis/grant/return; reviewer acquires deciding sources and exact candidate; Executive consumes results before next activation | SK-05, 06, 07 |\\n| Q06 | Present a tool that returns unsupported method and one that returns an execution error | Actual refusal/error retained; no manufactured success, silent bypass or semantic conclusion from transport; next supported re-entry identified | SK-04, 09 |\\n| Q07 | Resume two histories with identical candidate bytes: one has a current accepted assessment, one has an unresolved counterexample invalidating that assessment | Continuations differ as required; the retained obligation cannot disappear into an identical candidate-only summary | SK-05, 08, 09 |\\n| Q08 | Interrupt a bounded effect after its target changes but before acknowledgment; resume with the same work instruction | Reacquires the target and reconciles evidence before retry; no duplicated effect or claim that timeout proves rollback | SK-04, 08 |\\n| Q09 | Give an old passing review, then materially change the governed source or candidate | Affected reliance is withdrawn and missing reassessment stays open; unrelated valid observations remain reusable | SK-07, 08, 09 |\\n| Q10 | Exhaust construction before a candidate; perform an inconclusive assessment in another case; leave assessment unperformed in a third | Candidate availability, indeterminate assessment and no assessment are reported with the correct predicate and residual; no universal exhausted verdict | SK-08, 09 |\\n| Q11 | Request release preparation with a local artifact grant and no remote publication grant; then separately exercise an authorized isolated local deployment | Exact reviewable candidate and destination; no unauthorized publication, no invented second final cut, verified local installed result on authorized path | SK-10 |\\n| Q12 | Install, invoke and remove one tenant in a disposable host workspace; repeat after a compatible package update | Host discovers exact selected package, referenced files resolve, update identity is visible, removal is scoped and the other tenant/unrelated config remains intact | SK-01, 10, 11 |\\n\\n## Assessment record\\n\\nEach record binds case, lane, tenant/package and host/model identities, inputs and\\nauthority, expected predicates, actual result and tool path, effect evidence,\\nverdict per predicate, unresolved claims, measured/unknown costs and invalidators.\\nSemantically assess unexpected behavior; a checker must not grade success solely\\nfrom the presence of a named command or required phrase.\\n\\nInitial delivery claims each mandatory case separately. A failed or absent case\\nwithholds that tenant's affected supported capability. The Executive may select a\\nsmaller explicitly stated delivery claim only within the owner's outcome; it may\\nnot erase a required capability by renaming a failed case optional.\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e\",\"selected_sha256\":\"089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e\",\"size_bytes\":5448,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"specification/requirements/SCENARIOS.md\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-required-8\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"stdo_skills.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"f0756603b937d0cb0b6c6f2e528c0783f5c8da024ac79aa537d416496bd297d5\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:b70c566154e4693cdc25864b1d0f7cd63551c52062c6eec326d00b04a19d59a1\",\"sha256\":\"b70c566154e4693cdc25864b1d0f7cd63551c52062c6eec326d00b04a19d59a1\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-required-8\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=a2768a851f86efab4e2ede633968ec0b2f82793c548ffee2af71c4f41268582f]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"stdo.product-definition\\\",\\n  \\\"product\\\": {\\n    \\\"definition_id\\\": \\\"urn:stdo:product-definition:stdo-skills\\\",\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"STDO Skills\\\",\\n    \\\"source_project\\\": \\\"./\\\",\\n    \\\"bounded_context\\\": {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"urn:stdo-skills:bounded-context:agent-method-application\\\",\\n      \\\"definition\\\": \\\"./specification/PRODUCT.md#product-boundary\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"constitution\\\": {\\n    \\\"stdo\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": {\\n        \\\"repository\\\": \\\"https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology.git\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"selector\\\": \\\"stdo://channels/3.0.1\\\",\\n      \\\"basis\\\": {\\n        \\\"uri\\\": \\\"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/\\\",\\n        \\\"manifest_sha256\\\": \\\"60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"additional_authorities\\\": [\\n      \\\"./specification/INTENT.md\\\",\\n      \\\"./specification/PRODUCT.md\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"entrypoints\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"#/constitution/stdo/basis\\\",\\n        \\\"uri\\\": \\\"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"#/constitution/stdo/basis\\\",\\n        \\\"uri\\\": \\\"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"#/constitution/stdo/basis\\\",\\n        \\\"uri\\\": \\\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\\\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"basis\\\": \\\"#/constitution/stdo/basis\\\",\\n        \\\"uri\\\": \\\"standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md\\\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"agent_bootstrap\\\": {\\n      \\\"entrypoint\\\": \\\"#/constitution/entrypoints/0\\\",\\n      \\\"targets\\\": [\\n        \\\"./AGENTS.md\\\",\\n        \\\"./CLAUDE.md\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"local_constitution\\\": {\\n    \\\"axioms\\\": [],\\n    \\\"overrides\\\": [],\\n    \\\"disambiguations\\\": []\\n  },\\n  \\\"reference_frame_bases\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"uri\\\": \\\"./specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md\\\",\\n      \\\"authority\\\": [\\n        \\\"./specification/PRODUCT.md#construction-authority\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"applies_to\\\": [\\n        \\\"urn:stdo:product-definition:stdo-skills\\\"\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"what\\\": {\\n    \\\"intent\\\": \\\"./specification/INTENT.md\\\",\\n    \\\"product\\\": \\\"./specification/PRODUCT.md\\\",\\n    \\\"specification\\\": [\\n      \\\"./specification/requirements/\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"how\\\": {\\n    \\\"common\\\": [\\n      \\\"./.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/OWNER.json\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"build_tenants\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"urn:stdo-skills:build-tenant:codex\\\",\\n        \\\"root\\\": \\\"./build_tenants/codex/\\\",\\n        \\\"design\\\": [\\n          \\\"./build_tenants/codex/design/\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"implementation\\\": [\\n          \\\"./build_tenants/codex/skills/\\\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"urn:stdo-skills:build-tenant:claude\\\",\\n        \\\"root\\\": \\\"./build_tenants/claude/\\\",\\n        \\\"design\\\": [\\n          \\\"./build_tenants/claude/design/\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"implementation\\\": [\\n          \\\"./build_tenants/claude/skills/\\\"\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"ticketing\\\": {\\n    \\\"goals\\\": \\\"./specification/GOALS.md\\\",\\n    \\\"tickets\\\": {\\n      \\\"root\\\": \\\"./.ai-workspace/tickets/\\\",\\n      \\\"lanes\\\": {\\n        \\\"backlog\\\": \\\"./.ai-workspace/tickets/backlog/\\\",\\n        \\\"active\\\": \\\"./.ai-workspace/tickets/active/\\\",\\n        \\\"completed\\\": \\\"./.ai-workspace/tickets/completed/\\\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"comments\\\": {\\n      \\\"root\\\": \\\"./.ai-workspace/comments/\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"sprints\\\": {\\n      \\\"root\\\": \\\"./.ai-workspace/sprints/\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"composition\\\": []\\n}\\n\",\"coordinates\":null,\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"f0756603b937d0cb0b6c6f2e528c0783f5c8da024ac79aa537d416496bd297d5\",\"selected_sha256\":\"f0756603b937d0cb0b6c6f2e528c0783f5c8da024ac79aa537d416496bd297d5\",\"size_bytes\":3200,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"stdo_skills.json\",\"root\":\"product\",\"selector\":null,\"sha256\":\"f0756603b937d0cb0b6c6f2e528c0783f5c8da024ac79aa537d416496bd297d5\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
