{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-method-0\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"8152838639950b09389f99181172792100e4470b4807b4e112870cd4e6f6ba21\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[960,1000]}}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:81156e47c62ec96f95762822aaba09a1179b7336a00c1c6f603dcc6cc8845a85\",\"sha256\":\"81156e47c62ec96f95762822aaba09a1179b7336a00c1c6f603dcc6cc8845a85\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-method-0\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=d96f37613c091b8e40a8af2abf0f6f32c6f75eb23c2466834e5426d6299ba9cb]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Minimal activation binding\\n\\nThe following carrier-neutral content is sufficient to bind one declared\\nframe for one evaluation. It may be written in Markdown, structured data, a\\nprompt or another consumer-selected carrier without changing the relation\\n(P0, RF-016).\\n\\n```markdown\\n# Reference-Frame Activation: <stable activation identity>\\n\\n## Frame\\n- declaration identity and revision:\\n- exact evaluation and closed result algebra:\\n\\n## Subject And Basis\\n- exact subject or candidate identity:\\n- workspace, authority, dependency, configuration, and time basis:\\n\\n## Attention Surface\\n- material relations and applicable invariants:\\n- exact source and semantic references:\\n- explicit exclusions and prohibited assumptions:\\n\\n## Actor And Authority\\n- actor and capability envelope:\\n- semantic and evaluation authority:\\n- operation authority, subject, and territory where material:\\n- decision, acceptance, and publication authority:\\n\\n## Evidence And Relations\\n- admissible evidence and acquisition route:\\n- dependency, overlap, input, conjunction, or translation relations used:\\n- expected result consumer and return relation:\\n\\n## Stop And Change\\n- invalidation conditions:\\n- stop, residual, re-entry, and reconfiguration conditions:\\n```\\n\\nEvery field resolves through stable identities and source references.\\nPaths, line numbers, member counts, summaries and matching labels may aid\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[960,1000]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"8152838639950b09389f99181172792100e4470b4807b4e112870cd4e6f6ba21\",\"selected_sha256\":\"3c77753677f7f48707312ded4ad61993de943ef7dc2048955eaeeb159e8a0ab9\",\"size_bytes\":1379,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[960,1000]},\"sha256\":\"8152838639950b09389f99181172792100e4470b4807b4e112870cd4e6f6ba21\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-method-2\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[968,1055]}}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-method-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[402,435]}}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:0bbbe701f326500735386173be1843566456c74f58fb12eac0d71a5094fc80e0\",\"sha256\":\"0bbbe701f326500735386173be1843566456c74f58fb12eac0d71a5094fc80e0\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-method-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=7f165775142566dc22fd73480973ad5b6c8b6924cf9e62bc4584adbb96c54012]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Admission\\n\\nDrafting a step's contract and admitting it are distinct relations, even\\ninside one invocation that drafts, validates, admits and executes; no\\nseparate turn, carrier or approval ceremony is implied by the distinction.\\nA contract carries at minimum the states drafted, admitted, rejected and\\nsuperseded ([TICKETS §5](TICKETS.md#execution-contract-admission)).\\nExecution begins only after deterministic admission or an\\nexplicit human override of the exact contract. The drafting actor never\\ninfers admission from its own draft, from the presence of a carrier\\n(ticket, sprint entry, work contract), from lane placement or from an\\n`active` label. The admitted result identifies the admission mechanism and\\nits authority, the exact contract identity or digest, the decision and the\\nevidence, including any human override; absent those coordinates the\\ncontract stays drafted or rejected, and prose asserting admission is not\\nadmission evidence (P6; the actor cannot self-certify its own execution\\nbasis). Admission validates the contract against its cited outcome,\\nprerequisite or experiment basis; it does not admit that basis, and\\ndrafting, admitting or retaining a contract creates or renews no authority\\nits owner has not admitted (P6, P2;\\n[FOUNDATIONS §2 Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds), What\\ncreates no authority). Only an admitted contract activates a step: no\\nresult, child completion, tool output, model response, shared actor or\\nlateral handoff activates another step or authorises continuation by\\nitself, and a profile that routes results names its instances of this\\nrule. Purpose and material relation: these admission conditions govern every\\nconfiguration, and their generic owner is this section (P6).\\nThe admitted contract names one\\ndurable result and evidence surface; every result, withheld closure and\\nresidual obligation is recorded there before return, a conversation return\\nalone is not durable evidence, and if no such surface is authorised and\\navailable, admission refuses (P4b). Absent or rejected admission returns\\nthe missing work authority without execution, as `admission_refused` with\\nits cause ([§3 Admission and activation](#admission-and-activation)).\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[402,435]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"4d5bcdb267c104a1054eb52b2adc7bf4fc1ecdf8b17fb3878626a55e16b88705\",\"size_bytes\":2213,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[402,435]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-method-3\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"b39c45fd86b8f9add7d196b2974a8e5f75bf4a327cf796e362716a6b4f5776d5\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[985,1050]}}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-method-3\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"b39c45fd86b8f9add7d196b2974a8e5f75bf4a327cf796e362716a6b4f5776d5\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[985,1050]}}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:b473392b72c5a6a34518233bb702d408557728e6af85865825fea96f886e7b92\",\"sha256\":\"b473392b72c5a6a34518233bb702d408557728e6af85865825fea96f886e7b92\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-method-3\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=8d0bad7e8693e2a35afccb300a16833d11d967f0f5e7d988df2a077c55367788]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"- `F_D` classifies total deterministic processing under an exact traversal\\n  contract. An application declares `f_B:D_B->Outcome_B`, its closed logical\\n  domain, exact basis, all material computational state and dependencies,\\n  and its termination argument. For every domain input it terminates with\\n  exactly one declared outcome. Closed domains may be infinite when\\n  termination and outcome determination are established. Open-world\\n  semantic choice and undeclared clock, filesystem or global dependencies\\n  are outside this contract (P3, P4a, P6).\\n\\n  Here B is the exact basis of v, D_B is its declared logical input domain\\n  X_v (including material state and resource inputs), and Outcome_B is the\\n  declared result-or-stop domain Y_v | Omega_v. The function f_B determines\\n  one such outcome, including a stop with its closed report where declared;\\n  that report and its stop are not two outcomes. An enclosing step's output\\n  availability remains a separate predicate.\\n\\n  State-dependent processing declares input state and the meaning of its\\n  returned next state and value. Refusal and exhaustion retain their cause\\n  and evaluated predicate. The signature and traversal bind each stop to\\n  exactly one core value, never satisfied; an exhausted tag alone supplies\\n  no mapping. Construction availability and assessment retain their\\n  separate predicates and results, and an unperformed assessment has no\\n  result. A fuel-bounded operation is distinct from the potentially\\n  divergent operation it bounds. A deterministic decision or effect proposal\\n  establishes no physical completion, runtime admission, permission or\\n  quality (P5, P6; [ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#3-step-results-and-disposition)).\\n- `F_P` classifies bounded probabilistic interpretation, construction or\\n  proposal under an exact traversal contract. Its result has no semantic,\\n  admission, acceptance or closure authority merely because it is useful\\n  or repeatable (P6, P0; instance premise (iii) of §1 Foundation to law).\\n- `F_H` classifies explicit human adjudication under an exact identity,\\n  authority grant, subject, basis and decision contract. Human presence\\n  grants no ambient authority (P6).\\n\\nThe actor, the executor, the domain operation and the functor kind are\\ndifferent coordinates. `Encode`, `Interpret`, `Serialize`, `Measure` and\\nother named domain operations are not aliases for `F_D`, `F_P` or `F_H`.\\nDifferent traversals may share one functor kind without sharing identity,\\nsemantics, inputs, outputs, authority or evidence (P3, P6).\\n\\nClassifying an operation as F_D grants no semantic, evaluation, operation\\nor decision authority. This is the kind-specific application of\\n[AC-005](#ac-005-authority-conservation) and\\n[FOUNDATIONS Authority kinds](FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds): the exact\\noperation contract and admitted grant determine its permissions and\\nconsequences. Consumers apply this boundary to their own operations.\\n\\nEvaluation-operation profile. An operation declared to evaluate an unchanged\\nsubject identifies that subject, admissible reads, witness or log outputs,\\npermitted writes, stops and results, authority and invalidation conditions.\\nIt preserves the judged subject and does not perform the domain construction\\nit judges. Separately authorized persistence of a witness does not perform\\nthe judged domain construction. A construction or mutation needs its own\\noperation contract and grant; reporting a changed subject's property as the\\noriginal subject's property violates this evaluation contract (P6, P3).\\n\\nClosedness concerns dependencies material to the computation, not complete\\nworld knowledge. This kind's totality is stronger than total handling of\\nconditions in [ACTIVATION §4](ACTIVATION.md#4-totality-and-refinement).\\nUnbounded work is not automatically `F_P` when a totality argument is missing.\\nThe calculus does not classify every executable process as one of its kinds.\\nA new non-total deterministic process is outside qualifying F_D. A route to\\nan F_D claim is a separately identified bounded successor with its own\\ndomain, outcomes, dependency closure and termination argument; a fuel bound\\nis one possible construction. This proves nothing about the unbounded\\noriginal. Other work remains governed by its selected operation and execution\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[985,1050]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"b39c45fd86b8f9add7d196b2974a8e5f75bf4a327cf796e362716a6b4f5776d5\",\"selected_sha256\":\"a848f086fbed368139a61877431370267f3077d37eaf6b729163bf6707766053\",\"size_bytes\":4286,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[985,1050]},\"sha256\":\"b39c45fd86b8f9add7d196b2974a8e5f75bf4a327cf796e362716a6b4f5776d5\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-read-method-2\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\",\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[968,1055]}}}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:1b435ec7a7a50ea0d5c64ff2bdc785b389838909653da92b2d9a234a0a649b6f\",\"sha256\":\"1b435ec7a7a50ea0d5c64ff2bdc785b389838909653da92b2d9a234a0a649b6f\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-read-method-2\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=0da8b6195b7924b360e6c3c4aa7d6144dba042ae2995db2d9faf4bfb4794ba98]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"### Admission and activation\\n\\nA step exists only after its contract is admitted (§1, Admission) and its\\nframe is activated on the exact subject and basis (§2). The outcomes of\\nadmission and of context construction are owned here; each maps for the\\npredicate \\\"the step is lawfully admitted and activated on the exact\\nsubject and basis\\\", and its cause selects its value (P5, P6; RF-005 for\\nthe basis causes). The outcomes of frame activation are the `activate`\\nrefinement of [REFERENCE_FRAME §5](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#5-method-functions),\\nwhich owns their causes, their predicate and their core values. Because\\nthis predicate requires activation, a refused activation decides it with\\nthe value REFERENCE_FRAME §5 gives; the table names those outcomes and\\nmaps none of them again:\\n\\n| Outcome | Cause | Core value |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `activated` | the contract is admitted with its admission evidence (§1), Z, R, the required-edge semantics, the basis and the scope are exact and the material closure is finite and unique (§2, step 1), its projection returns a selected context (§2, step 2), and activation returns `activated_frame` | satisfied |\\n| `admission_refused(authority)` | the work authority the step needs is not admitted: no admission mechanism or explicit human override admits the exact contract, or no durable result and evidence surface is authorised and available; the outcome names the missing authority or surface and its owner | out_of_frame |\\n| `admission_refused(basis)` | the contract's cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis, or the exact subject and basis it names, cannot support it; the outcome names that basis | invalid_basis |\\n| `closure_unresolved` | the seed set Z, the relation family R, the required-edge semantics, the basis or the scope is not exact, or the material closure is not finite and unique on the exact basis (§2, step 1; AC-010), or the projection of the closure returns a gap or refusal (§2, step 2; AC-011); the outcome names the condition that fails and the basis coordinates that leave it open | invalid_basis |\\n| `out_of_frame` | no available frame and actor pairing declares a material relation or capability the evaluation needs (§2, Activation), or no fit option of §2 step 3 fits the selected context to an actor's envelope | out_of_frame |\\n| `activation_refusal` with its cause | a cause REFERENCE_FRAME §5 states | the core value REFERENCE_FRAME §5 maps that cause to |\\n\\nThese outcomes are not values of construction availability and are not\\nresults of a step. A refused admission or activation creates no step, no\\nactivation of the step's frame and no work result, the closed output of a\\nconstructing actor to its consumer; the outcome returns to the assigning\\nauthority or the declared result carrier, and no consumer records it as a\\nstep's stop state. [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §5](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#work-result)\\napplies this rule to the Worker.\\nPurpose and material relation: a mismatch known before the step begins is\\nreported with its cause in the one core, so it is neither mistaken for a\\nstep that stopped nor for one that ran.\\n\\n### Construction availability\\n\\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\\nexists (P5, P6):\\n\\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\\n\\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\\n\\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\\n\\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \\\"a candidate is available\\\", never\\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\\n(P5, P6).\\n\\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\\n(P6).\\n\\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\\nP3).\\n\\n### Disposition\\n\\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\\nsemantic dispositions (§1, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\\n([EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[968,1055]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selected_sha256\":\"6c24e1fcc0e34e19e8a6fce27ad866bf11bb488487442f1adc48b995c9833ef7\",\"size_bytes\":6393,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[968,1055]},\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"The exact STDO v3.0.1-rc.1 installation verified successfully, and I’ve acquired the required sources. I’m building one discoverable skill with task-specific references. Actual host trials and independent review remain separate from this construction result.\n\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-write-design-001\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"work.write\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"grant_id\\\":\\\"urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:1\\\",\\\"target\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"build_tenants/codex/design/DESIGN.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null},\\\"mode\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"record\\\":{\\\"provenance\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"operator\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"codex/TASK.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"eae576ac13cbf358889845b6532c62482d0cc593d9c669eb467a88911d01a9e0\\\",\\\"selector\\\":null},\\\"text\\\":\\\"# Codex tenant design — T001 candidate 1\\\\n\\\\nRecorded before implementation. Scope: build_tenants/codex only; construction authority is operator codex/TASK.md SHA256 eae576ac13cbf358889845b6532c62482d0cc593d9c669eb467a88911d01a9e0, grant urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:1. No Product acceptance, publication or installation is claimed.\\\\n\\\\n## Basis and source ownership\\\\n\\\\nSTDO Skills common inventory a6d348b8385ea453ce29362fb9d74559304b1b91743b3c9ea31a83a9f02b5f2d governs this candidate. STDO stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/ manifest 60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8 owns the method. Its installed basis was verified by stdo status --definition stdo_skills.json --verify on 2026-10-25. The discovery channel does not select a newer basis.\\\\n\\\\nRequirements SHA256 dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc and scenarios SHA256 089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e remain common external authority. The frame basis SHA256 00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa is selected by this activation for construction, not accepted by this Worker. Method routing comes from specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md SHA256 15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3. Installed deciding sections are acquired as needed; no copied methodology is installed.\\\\n\\\\n## Algorithm and host binding\\\\n\\\\nOne skill, stdo-work, supplies task-based discovery for an already governed workspace and explicit setup requests. Its name and description remain available to Codex; automatic invocation stays enabled by omitting any disabling policy. Only the entrypoint and the relevant reference are acquired. References are packaged inside the skill, so copying the complete directory preserves their links.\\\\n\\\\n| Requirements | Algorithm | Codex or tool mechanism | Finite proof |\\\\n|---|---|---|---|\\\\n| SK-01 | Route relevant task, ignore unrelated task, distinguish discovery from execution | SKILL.md frontmatter; repository .agents/skills/stdo-work; explicit \"'$stdo-work | Q01, Q02, Q12 |'\"\\\\n| SK-02 | Select one Product, verify exact installed basis, acquire bootstrap and deciding owner | stdo status --definition PATH --verify; public source.read with exact SourceRefs | Q03 |\\\\n| SK-03 | Reuse sufficient authority; choose direct Writer for a sufficient small effect; coordinate only on material boundary | Codex reasoning over acquired contract; host actors only where selected and admitted | Q04, Q05 |\\\\n| SK-04 | Discover exact schemas, call required operation, retain actual response and effect evidence | native a_c public MCP or explicitly configured CLI using complete request envelopes | Q01, Q06, Q08 |\\\\n| SK-05 | Preserve smallest deciding causal context including retained obligations and differing histories | exact SourceRefs, context.assemble when selected; activation carrier | Q05, Q07 |\\\\n| SK-06 | Bind child outcome, basis, territory, proof, consumer and stop; consume closed return before next activation | configured contract.preflight, dispatch.start/observe and return.capture/check where admitted; no invented tool | Q04, Q05 |\\\\n| SK-07 | Derive expected behavior from source before exact candidate; retain exposure and family limits | review.prepare where selected; fresh separately admitted reviewer; source.read | Q05, Q09 |\\\\n| SK-08 | Reacquire current evidence, reconcile uncertain effects before retry, retain unaffected evidence | workspace.observe, source.read, evidence.read, granted recovery path | Q07-Q10 |\\\\n| SK-09 | Separate candidate availability, assessment, consumer disposition, acceptance | declared closed return schema, original basis, explicit residuals and not_performed | Q06, Q09, Q10 |\\\\n| SK-10 | Prepare exact immutable candidate; act only on authorized release destination; scoped package install/update/remove | selected release tool discovered from its contract; file-copy deployment only with corresponding grant | Q11, Q12 |\\\\n| SK-11 | Package references together; inventory exact content; retain previous identity on update | read-only package verifier; owned-directory installation recipe | Q12 |\\\\n| SK-12 | Freeze substantive tasks and independent oracle, preserve every attempt and unknown costs | qualification plan and actual host traces, not keyword success grading | Q01-Q12 |\\\\n\\\\nCodex mechanics are independently sourced in operator codex/HOST.md SHA256 6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e: codex-cli 0.164.0, repository-local .agents/skills discovery, explicit \"'$skill-name, relative references, restart when discovery is stale. Configured model/effort gpt-6-astra/max is inherited; actual resolution is unknown unless the run records it. No nested actor is launched in this construction.'\"\\\\n\\\\n## Tool boundary and failure behavior\\\\n\\\\nNative method profile urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1 SHA256 a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7 is selected. tools.describe reports provisional construction support, not qualification. Its builder identity v2.5.1-rc.2 is distinct from this selected operation binding. There is no supported native results.conjoin. Executive consumption is F_P under its granted relation; any decision must preserve required predicates, applicability, incompatible bases and unresolved contradictions.\\\\n\\\\nHost reads, SHA256 computation and static package checks are declared auxiliary mechanics. They establish byte/structure facts only and never replace required source.read, workspace.observe, work.write, admission or assessment results. All current construction deliverables are written with work.write, own observation and exact preimage; postimage and OperationEvidence are then read. Unknown completion stops dependent writing pending reconciliation.\\\\n\\\\nA failed required operation withholds its dependent claim. Independent work can continue under its existing grant. No automatic retries, authorization renewal or publication follow from successful transport. A missing installation or ambiguous Product is a basis problem, not a request to adopt latest. An unperformed assessment has no core result; performed inconclusive assessment is indeterminate; construction without an output is incomplete for candidate availability.\\\\n\\\\n## Installation and qualification\\\\n\\\\nREADME supplies a repository-local, single-directory copy recipe and explicit update/removal custody checks. No installer mutates host configuration implicitly. A read-only verifier checks packaged resources and optional observed inventory. It does not assess instruction semantics or host discovery.\\\\n\\\\nQ01-Q12 actual host trials, source-first independent assessment, release and owner acceptance remain unperformed here. The qualification plan keeps each case/lane visible and preserves failures. Static checks support only packaging integrity; they do not justify automatic-selection reliability or efficiency claims.\\\\n\\\"},\\\"interpretation\\\":null,\\\"observations\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"sha256:bc7a4520c234dfc11e9c668f4b7c6d6f2a8180dfd48f4a665b2db1fed248256b\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"bc7a4520c234dfc11e9c668f4b7c6d6f2a8180dfd48f4a665b2db1fed248256b\\\"}]}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/codex/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 6c73ef4eff91f018a79fa5edba57fb6e788d609c4c95e3905059c0a22db9349c --principal codex call --request /dev/stdin <<'AC_REQUEST'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"codex-T001-write-design-001\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"work.write\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"grant_id\\\":\\\"urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:1\\\",\\\"target\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"product\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"build_tenants/codex/design/DESIGN.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":null,\\\"selector\\\":null},\\\"mode\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"record\\\":{\\\"provenance\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"root\\\":\\\"operator\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"codex/TASK.md\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"eae576ac13cbf358889845b6532c62482d0cc593d9c669eb467a88911d01a9e0\\\",\\\"selector\\\":null},\\\"text\\\":\\\"# Codex tenant design — T001 candidate 1\\\\n\\\\nRecorded before implementation. Scope: build_tenants/codex only; construction authority is operator codex/TASK.md SHA256 eae576ac13cbf358889845b6532c62482d0cc593d9c669eb467a88911d01a9e0, grant urn:stdo-skills:T001:codex:construction:1. No Product acceptance, publication or installation is claimed.\\\\n\\\\n## Basis and source ownership\\\\n\\\\nSTDO Skills common inventory a6d348b8385ea453ce29362fb9d74559304b1b91743b3c9ea31a83a9f02b5f2d governs this candidate. STDO stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/ manifest 60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8 owns the method. Its installed basis was verified by stdo status --definition stdo_skills.json --verify on 2026-10-25. The discovery channel does not select a newer basis.\\\\n\\\\nRequirements SHA256 dcc2564e597d3d3c8fcff025a515f4a92a62e7f3aa2f7ba80af97f7db75f6acc and scenarios SHA256 089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e remain common external authority. The frame basis SHA256 00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa is selected by this activation for construction, not accepted by this Worker. Method routing comes from specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md SHA256 15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3. Installed deciding sections are acquired as needed; no copied methodology is installed.\\\\n\\\\n## Algorithm and host binding\\\\n\\\\nOne skill, stdo-work, supplies task-based discovery for an already governed workspace and explicit setup requests. Its name and description remain available to Codex; automatic invocation stays enabled by omitting any disabling policy. Only the entrypoint and the relevant reference are acquired. References are packaged inside the skill, so copying the complete directory preserves their links.\\\\n\\\\n| Requirements | Algorithm | Codex or tool mechanism | Finite proof |\\\\n|---|---|---|---|\\\\n| SK-01 | Route relevant task, ignore unrelated task, distinguish discovery from execution | SKILL.md frontmatter; repository .agents/skills/stdo-work; explicit \"'$stdo-work | Q01, Q02, Q12 |'\"\\\\n| SK-02 | Select one Product, verify exact installed basis, acquire bootstrap and deciding owner | stdo status --definition PATH --verify; public source.read with exact SourceRefs | Q03 |\\\\n| SK-03 | Reuse sufficient authority; choose direct Writer for a sufficient small effect; coordinate only on material boundary | Codex reasoning over acquired contract; host actors only where selected and admitted | Q04, Q05 |\\\\n| SK-04 | Discover exact schemas, call required operation, retain actual response and effect evidence | native a_c public MCP or explicitly configured CLI using complete request envelopes | Q01, Q06, Q08 |\\\\n| SK-05 | Preserve smallest deciding causal context including retained obligations and differing histories | exact SourceRefs, context.assemble when selected; activation carrier | Q05, Q07 |\\\\n| SK-06 | Bind child outcome, basis, territory, proof, consumer and stop; consume closed return before next activation | configured contract.preflight, dispatch.start/observe and return.capture/check where admitted; no invented tool | Q04, Q05 |\\\\n| SK-07 | Derive expected behavior from source before exact candidate; retain exposure and family limits | review.prepare where selected; fresh separately admitted reviewer; source.read | Q05, Q09 |\\\\n| SK-08 | Reacquire current evidence, reconcile uncertain effects before retry, retain unaffected evidence | workspace.observe, source.read, evidence.read, granted recovery path | Q07-Q10 |\\\\n| SK-09 | Separate candidate availability, assessment, consumer disposition, acceptance | declared closed return schema, original basis, explicit residuals and not_performed | Q06, Q09, Q10 |\\\\n| SK-10 | Prepare exact immutable candidate; act only on authorized release destination; scoped package install/update/remove | selected release tool discovered from its contract; file-copy deployment only with corresponding grant | Q11, Q12 |\\\\n| SK-11 | Package references together; inventory exact content; retain previous identity on update | read-only package verifier; owned-directory installation recipe | Q12 |\\\\n| SK-12 | Freeze substantive tasks and independent oracle, preserve every attempt and unknown costs | qualification plan and actual host traces, not keyword success grading | Q01-Q12 |\\\\n\\\\nCodex mechanics are independently sourced in operator codex/HOST.md SHA256 6f940ea5514cf8ea3e0b359adbb0337d3ff020c414aca54c502befab9665213e: codex-cli 0.164.0, repository-local .agents/skills discovery, explicit \"'$skill-name, relative references, restart when discovery is stale. Configured model/effort gpt-6-astra/max is inherited; actual resolution is unknown unless the run records it. No nested actor is launched in this construction.'\"\\\\n\\\\n## Tool boundary and failure behavior\\\\n\\\\nNative method profile urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1 SHA256 a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7 is selected. tools.describe reports provisional construction support, not qualification. Its builder identity v2.5.1-rc.2 is distinct from this selected operation binding. There is no supported native results.conjoin. Executive consumption is F_P under its granted relation; any decision must preserve required predicates, applicability, incompatible bases and unresolved contradictions.\\\\n\\\\nHost reads, SHA256 computation and static package checks are declared auxiliary mechanics. They establish byte/structure facts only and never replace required source.read, workspace.observe, work.write, admission or assessment results. All current construction deliverables are written with work.write, own observation and exact preimage; postimage and OperationEvidence are then read. Unknown completion stops dependent writing pending reconciliation.\\\\n\\\\nA failed required operation withholds its dependent claim. Independent work can continue under its existing grant. No automatic retries, authorization renewal or publication follow from successful transport. A missing installation or ambiguous Product is a basis problem, not a request to adopt latest. An unperformed assessment has no core result; performed inconclusive assessment is indeterminate; construction without an output is incomplete for candidate availability.\\\\n\\\\n## Installation and qualification\\\\n\\\\nREADME supplies a repository-local, single-directory copy recipe and explicit update/removal custody checks. No installer mutates host configuration implicitly. A read-only verifier checks packaged resources and optional observed inventory. It does not assess instruction semantics or host discovery.\\\\n\\\\nQ01-Q12 actual host trials, source-first independent assessment, release and owner acceptance remain unperformed here. The qualification plan keeps each case/lane visible and preserves failures. Static checks support only packaging integrity; they do not justify automatic-selection reliability or efficiency claims.\\\\n\\\"},\\\"interpretation\\\":null,\\\"observations\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"sha256:bc7a4520c234dfc11e9c668f4b7c6d6f2a8180dfd48f4a665b2db1fed248256b\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"bc7a4520c234dfc11e9c668f4b7c6d6f2a8180dfd48f4a665b2db1fed248256b\\\"}]}}\nAC_REQUEST\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:2cc76eb6958566e5c357d26eac85e4a543e73ac44ce095a0014ffc3f10aefc4d\",\"sha256\":\"2cc76eb6958566e5c357d26eac85e4a543e73ac44ce095a0014ffc3f10aefc4d\"},\"id\":\"codex-T001-write-design-001\",\"operation\":\"work.write\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"source_missing\",\"core_value\":\"invalid_basis\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(work.write): declared exact output/effect-evidence payload availability on the requested basis\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"refused(basis)\"},\"refusal\":{\"code\":\"source_missing\",\"gaps\":[],\"reason\":\"Missing path component: /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/build_tenants/codex\",\"source_refs\":[]},\"result\":null,\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"refused\"}\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
